# Memory's own environment. scripts/startup/derive-env.sh generates
# services/memory/.env from the platform .env on every startup; this file
# documents what it holds. Memory names no Core database host or credential
# (Durable Agent Session Record REQ-02).
PGHOST=memory-postgres
PGPORT=5432
PGUSER=memory
# From the platform .env's MEMORY_PGPASSWORD.
PGPASSWORD=
PGDATABASE=memory
# The same role, password and database for memory-postgres itself (the
# postgres image reads these, not the PG* names above). Its compose file
# interpolates nothing from the caller's environment.
POSTGRES_USER=memory
# From the platform .env's MEMORY_PGPASSWORD.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
POSTGRES_DB=memory
# From the platform .env's MEMORY_DJANGO_SECRET_KEY.
DJANGO_SECRET_KEY=
# Not carried by the generated file. memory/settings.py reads these from the
# process environment, defaulting as shown; derive-env.sh writes none of them
# and replaces services/memory/.env in full on every startup. Most are not
# set by any `environment:` entry in docker-compose.yml; the exceptions are
# MEMORY_EXTRACTION_SPOOL, MEMORY_API_URL and MEMORY_PLATFORM_CORPUS_ROOT,
# which compose sets (noted where they appear below). A value added to .env
# by hand reaches Memory's containers (each takes `env_file: .env`) once they
# are recreated, and holds only until the next startup regenerates the file;
# otherwise a deployment runs with the defaults. Apart from the three compose
# sets and MEMORY_EMBED_MODEL_DIR (set by the Dockerfile's ENV in the image and
# by run_tests.sh for the suite), in this repository only the tests set them
# (by overriding the settings or passing them to a subprocess,
# tests/test_copier_process.py).
# The reconciling pass's interval must stay below the 35-minute quiet
# interval; Memory refuses to start otherwise.
# MEMORY_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_SECONDS=1800
# MEMORY_WATCHER_ENABLED=true
# MEMORY_QUIET_SWEEP_SECONDS=60
# Artifact text extraction (memory-extraction; artifact-text-extraction.md).
# Core's artifact read surface and Redis, as the ai-gang network names them.
# MEMORY_CORE_URL=http://core:9100
# MEMORY_REDIS_URL=redis://ai-gang-redis:6379
# The spool memory-extraction shares with memory-extractor (set by
# docker-compose.yml's environment entry).
# MEMORY_EXTRACTION_SPOOL=/var/lib/aigang/memory/extraction-spool
# REQ-06's declared time limit for one file, and REQ-04's sweep interval.
# MEMORY_EXTRACTION_TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS=120
# MEMORY_EXTRACTION_SWEEP_SECONDS=1800
# Attempts ending without a result before a file is recorded as a failure.
# MEMORY_EXTRACTION_ATTEMPT_LIMIT=3
# MEMORY_EXTRACTION_GRACE_SECONDS=30
# MEMORY_EXTRACTION_WORKER_ID=
# Corpus indexing (memory-indexer; corpus-indexing.md). memory-api's reads
# and the platform corpus's mount are set by docker-compose.yml's
# environment entry.
# MEMORY_API_URL=http://memory-api:9200
# MEMORY_PLATFORM_CORPUS_ROOT=/platform-source
# How often the archive's session listing and notes read are followed, and
# the extraction record compared with the index (seconds).
# MEMORY_INDEX_ARCHIVE_FOLLOW_SECONDS=5
# MEMORY_INDEX_LIBRARY_FOLLOW_SECONDS=5
# How often a new project's work-item event stream is looked for.
# MEMORY_INDEX_STREAM_DISCOVERY_SECONDS=30
# How often recorded indexing failures are retried (REQ-09).
# MEMORY_INDEX_RETRY_SECONDS=300
# MEMORY_INDEX_CONSUMER=
# The embedding model, baked into the image at build time and never
# downloaded (memory-indexer and memory-api). Threads per process; 0 = all.
# MEMORY_EMBED_MODEL_DIR=/opt/memory-embedding-model
# MEMORY_EMBED_THREADS=0
# Knowledge retrieval (memory-api's /retrieve; knowledge-retrieval.md). It
# reads Core (MEMORY_CORE_URL) and Redis (MEMORY_REDIS_URL), above, at query
# time. How long one status read of Core may take (seconds).
# MEMORY_RETRIEVAL_STATUS_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=10
